---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../../site.config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy · ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description="Detour privacy policy — what stays on your device, what we do not collect, and how to contact the maintainers."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <main class="legal">
    <div class="wrap legal__inner">
      <header class="legal__head">
        <p class="legal__eyebrow">Policy</p>
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p class="legal__meta">
          <strong>Detour</strong> (“{siteConfig.tagline}”) · Effective 2026-10-07
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Detour is a browser extension that runs on your device. It is free, MIT-licensed software.
          The project does not operate an account system or a server for the extension.
        </p>

        <h2>Data that stays on your device</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Rules you write or import (including redirects, headers, injected code, mocks, and
            replacement bodies)
          </li>
          <li>Whether Detour is on, theme, and badge preference</li>
          <li>The apply report (which rules were installed or refused)</li>
          <li>
            A session match log: up to 50 rows with a rule label and URL. It is cleared when the
            browser session ends. It does not include rule bodies
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Firefox’s manifest declares data collection as <strong>none</strong>.</p>

        <h2>What we do not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No account, sign-in, or cloud sync</li>
          <li>
            No telemetry. The extension does not send rule bodies, file contents, or the match log
            anywhere
          </li>
          <li>No sale of personal information</li>
          <li>
            The <code>debugger</code> permission (Chrome) and response filtering (Firefox) change
            responses locally after you allow them. They are not used to transmit page contents to us
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>
          {siteConfig.url} is a static product site. Standard CDN and edge logs (IP, user agent,
          timestamps) may be retained briefly for security and reliability. There is no account form
          and no analytics product embedded by Detour on this site.
        </p>

        <h2>Permissions</h2>
        <p>
          Chrome, Edge, and Firefox show the extension’s permissions at install. Rationale lives with
          the source in
          <a href={`${siteConfig.github}/blob/main/docs/distribution/permissions.md`}
            >docs/distribution/permissions.md</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions:
          <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>
          ·
          <a href={siteConfig.github}>github.com/protovoid/detour</a>
          ·
          <a href="/">detour.protovoid.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 5rem) 0 var(--space-8);
  }

  .legal__inner {
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .legal__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .legal__head h1 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.4rem + 2vw, 2.75rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .legal__meta {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
  }

  .prose li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .prose code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
